WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.254
- My grandmother survived the Holocaust

00:00:02.254 --> 00:00:05.720
in the most badass way
and this is that story.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.285
(light music)

00:00:08.285 --> 00:00:12.749
She was a teenager when the
Nazis started to invade Poland.

00:00:12.749 --> 00:00:15.532
This one older guy had the
hots for my grandmother

00:00:15.532 --> 00:00:17.962
and he wanted this
special suit to be made.

00:00:17.962 --> 00:00:20.222
This guy who needed a suit was well off.

00:00:20.222 --> 00:00:21.869
His name was Leon.

00:00:21.869 --> 00:00:26.036
So she suggested that he go to
her father, who was a tailor.

00:00:27.385 --> 00:00:30.173
He asked my great-grandfather, the tailor,

00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:32.628
to make him a suit with a special pockets

00:00:32.628 --> 00:00:36.187
so he could hide jewelry and money.

00:00:36.187 --> 00:00:38.673
My grandmother was pretty
popular at the time,

00:00:38.673 --> 00:00:41.093
so she kind of strung him along a bit.

00:00:41.093 --> 00:00:43.166
She always said that she had noticed

00:00:43.166 --> 00:00:46.511
that he had really big
hands and really nice teeth.

00:00:46.511 --> 00:00:49.815
Apparently, this guy was
kind of a lady's man.

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:52.982
We're not really sure who pursued who.

00:00:54.057 --> 00:00:57.295
Sometime after September 1939,

00:00:57.295 --> 00:00:59.045
her family and friends were forced

00:00:59.045 --> 00:01:01.783
into a work camp in Poland.

00:01:01.783 --> 00:01:05.115
Despite the harsh conditions,
her relationship with Leon

00:01:05.115 --> 00:01:06.624
continued to grow.

00:01:06.624 --> 00:01:11.137
In late 1943, everyone was
moved to a different camp,

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.887
specifically Majowka.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.398
One day, the German officers gave shovels

00:01:17.398 --> 00:01:21.639
to my grandmother, her friends,
family, and 300 other people

00:01:21.639 --> 00:01:23.907
so they could start digging their graves.

00:01:23.907 --> 00:01:25.763
The plan was to shoot them all

00:01:25.763 --> 00:01:28.629
so they would fall into
the graves that they dug.

00:01:28.629 --> 00:01:30.973
My grandmother was not having it.

00:01:30.973 --> 00:01:32.959
She jumped on the officer's back.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.237
His name was Schraff.

00:01:34.237 --> 00:01:35.806
And started choking him.

00:01:35.806 --> 00:01:39.919
Keep in mind, she was
19 or 20 at this time.

00:01:39.919 --> 00:01:41.546
Like I said, badass.

00:01:41.546 --> 00:01:43.987
She always made a point to say

00:01:43.987 --> 00:01:46.914
that she dug her
fingernails into his neck.

00:01:46.914 --> 00:01:50.029
In the midst of the fight,
he wrestled her to the ground

00:01:50.029 --> 00:01:52.112
and shot her in the head.

00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:55.498
But what Schraff didn't know

00:01:55.498 --> 00:01:58.235
was that the bullet just
grazed her forehead.

00:01:58.235 --> 00:02:02.635
There was lots of blood,
but she played dead.

00:02:02.635 --> 00:02:05.844
Suddenly, there was an
air raid or something

00:02:05.844 --> 00:02:07.525
and the officers got distracted.

00:02:07.525 --> 00:02:10.548
Everyone, prisoners and officers alike,

00:02:10.548 --> 00:02:12.276
ended up going back to the barracks.

00:02:12.276 --> 00:02:15.151
So, no one ended up
getting killed that day.

00:02:15.151 --> 00:02:18.157
My grandmother stayed there,
bleeding, for a long time.

00:02:18.157 --> 00:02:20.490
She claims it was all night.

00:02:21.671 --> 00:02:24.145
Then, she went back to the barracks

00:02:24.145 --> 00:02:27.402
and was like, "Surprise, I'm alive."

00:02:27.402 --> 00:02:30.188
Everyone she was with ended up hiding her

00:02:30.188 --> 00:02:31.468
under the barracks.

00:02:31.468 --> 00:02:33.973
The next day, while on patrol,

00:02:33.973 --> 00:02:37.188
the guards noticed my grandmother's body

00:02:37.188 --> 00:02:38.807
wasn't where they had left her.

00:02:38.807 --> 00:02:40.902
They knew she was hiding.

00:02:40.902 --> 00:02:43.536
"Give her to us, or else
we'll kill all of you."

00:02:43.536 --> 00:02:45.833
So, of course, they give her up

00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:47.589
and the guards beat her up some more.

00:02:47.589 --> 00:02:50.065
From there, she was put in a jail

00:02:50.065 --> 00:02:54.209
and a high-ranking officer
was threatening to kill her.

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:57.459
As all hope seemed lost, in comes Leon.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.933
He bribes the commander with jewelry,

00:03:01.933 --> 00:03:06.277
specifically a diamond he had
hidden in his secret pockets

00:03:06.277 --> 00:03:08.534
that was sewn in by her father.

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.701
This bribe saved her life.

00:03:11.847 --> 00:03:14.080
On a different night, Schraff,

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.892
the man who attempted
to kill my grandmother,

00:03:16.892 --> 00:03:18.280
was drunk at the barracks.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:22.014
He was waving his gun, saying
he was gonna shoot everyone.

00:03:22.014 --> 00:03:24.502
Now, my grandmother was really sharp.

00:03:24.502 --> 00:03:25.818
She knew high German.

00:03:25.818 --> 00:03:29.472
So, she was always able to
communicate with the Nazis.

00:03:29.472 --> 00:03:32.252
Even though she didn't go
through all her schooling,

00:03:32.252 --> 00:03:35.424
she was pretty much
fluent in five languages:

00:03:35.424 --> 00:03:39.377
German, Polish, English,
Yiddish, and Hebrew.

00:03:39.377 --> 00:03:41.494
She was able to use this to her advantage

00:03:41.494 --> 00:03:44.228
because she was able to calm Schraff down.

00:03:44.228 --> 00:03:45.821
He ended up leaving the barracks

00:03:45.821 --> 00:03:49.195
without killing anyone that night.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:52.350
Some time passes and
everyone in the barracks,

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:55.675
including Leon, is sent
off to various camps.

00:03:55.675 --> 00:03:59.842
My grandmother and her family
were deported to Auschwitz.

00:04:01.098 --> 00:04:03.164
Once there, her brother and father

00:04:03.164 --> 00:04:05.111
get sent to Buna Werke Camp.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:09.278
In January 1945, her and her
mother march to Ravensbruck.

00:04:11.555 --> 00:04:14.282
Her mother gets ill after the march

00:04:14.282 --> 00:04:16.219
and ends up in the infirmary.

00:04:16.219 --> 00:04:18.534
My grandmother visits her every day.

00:04:18.534 --> 00:04:21.240
She knew her mother was close to death,

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.476
so she cut off a lock of her hair.

00:04:23.476 --> 00:04:26.439
The next day, when she
went back to the infirmary,

00:04:26.439 --> 00:04:28.106
her mother was gone.

00:04:29.796 --> 00:04:32.765
My grandmother kept that lock of hair

00:04:32.765 --> 00:04:36.432
in a locket she always
wore around her neck.

00:04:38.208 --> 00:04:40.154
Fast forward to the end of the war

00:04:40.154 --> 00:04:41.919
and the camps get liberated.

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:44.169
(cheering)

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:48.838
My grandmother ends up in
Sweden with the Red Cross.

00:04:48.838 --> 00:04:51.225
She learns that Leon had survived

00:04:51.225 --> 00:04:53.341
and was in a hospital in Germany.

00:04:53.341 --> 00:04:57.766
She finds out that her
brother and father had died.

00:04:57.766 --> 00:04:59.360
So she tracks down Leon.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.973
She finds him and meets his
remaining family in Berlin.

00:05:03.973 --> 00:05:06.049
And they get married.

00:05:06.049 --> 00:05:09.073
Shortly after, in 1947, they move

00:05:09.073 --> 00:05:11.573
to Charleston, South Carolina.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:16.205
They had six kids, one
of which is my father.

00:05:16.205 --> 00:05:18.928
My grandfather owned a bunch of businesses

00:05:18.928 --> 00:05:21.693
and my grandmother owned
a dressmaking shop.

00:05:21.693 --> 00:05:25.660
They were together until my
grandfather died in 1973.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.505
My grandmother actually went to court

00:05:27.505 --> 00:05:31.957
to testify against Schraff
and helped put him away.

00:05:31.957 --> 00:05:34.457
(light music)

00:05:44.685 --> 00:05:48.852
- [Interviewer] Would you
tell me your name, please?

00:06:11.815 --> 00:06:14.063
(squeaking)

